<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistan forex reserves rise to $1.808 bln.</title>
<headline>Pakistan forex reserves rise to $1.808 bln.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-03-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's foreign exchange reserves rose to $1.808 billion dollar on March 15 from 1.711 billion on March 8, compared to $2.046 billion a year ago, the State (central) Bank of Pakistan said on Thursday.</p>
<p>Following is the weekly foreign exchange reserves holding position in Pakistan:</p>
<p>    (BLN DLRS)	    MARCH 15   MARCH 8   MARCH 14,1996</p>
<p> TOTAL			1.808	1.711     2.046</p>
<p> Forex in Pakistan	0.636	0.745     0.884</p>
<p> Forex outside Pakistan 0.493	0.288     0.453</p>
<p> Gold coins and bullion 0.676	0.676     0.701</p>
<p> Special Drawing Rights 0.002	0.002     0.007</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
</text>
